      "content": "Ah, the fickle nature of your levain is much like a mischievous goblin, isn't it? You know, these little critters, much like your levain, can be quite temperamental. They thrive in the right conditions, but a slight change in the environment can send them into a frenzy. Your kitchen's ambient temperature is like the goblin's favorite playground—too warm, and they get hyperactive, too cold, and they're sluggish. It's all about finding that sweet spot where your levain can settle down and become a reliable friend, not a wild beast.\n\nAs for the protein content in your rye/AP mix, think of it as the goblin's diet. Too much protein, and they're bound to get a bit too wild, causing your pH levels to swing like a pendulum. But if you balance it just right, your levain will be more like a well-behaved goblin, content and stable. So, maybe it's time to tweak your recipe, just like a wise goblin would adjust his diet to keep his antics in check. And remember, just like with goblins, patience is key. Give your levain some time to find its groove, and soon you'll have a stable",
